{"id": "EUVD-2026-86103", "enisaUuid": "49a10995-5182-3f6b-88b9-5c84e9211158", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI/sysfs: Add CAP_SYS_ADMIN check to __resource_resize_store()\n\nCurrently, the __resource_resize_store() allows writing to the\nresourceN_resize sysfs attribute to change a BAR's size without checking\nfor capabilities, currently relying only on the file access check.\n\nResizing a BAR modifies PCI device configuration and can disrupt active\ndrivers.  After the upcoming conversion to static attributes, it will also\ntrigger resource file updates via sysfs_update_groups().\n\nAdd a CAP_SYS_ADMIN check to prevent unprivileged users from performing BAR\nresize operations.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d02dd7ce8e52b66b7d3b6eca2a7d81e7f5b10a62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b722a607f858b9cd036075ea0efad553fb98e982", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbf0628c0b7db86c5ce36451f088101546acbf1d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25ec7f57deceec633f27bc93b615f951e2ade814"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97505", "GHSA-6xm8-36mh-mxj7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21349986-9473-35bc-b8c7-dc849f7a0edb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "4f1cebc5-a8d2-3816-b6d9-b9d49cb3f78d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "6fe17c20-bc39-3c76-962c-36b29addc87c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "99b7ba19-be7a-37b7-889d-91061bead09e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91fa127794ac1c48069479b9d45eb4c7378c0e30 <25ec7f57deceec633f27bc93b615f951e2ade814"}, {"id": "ab0812e2-4bde-362d-99c5-db9b3ba096bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91fa127794ac1c48069479b9d45eb4c7378c0e30 <d02dd7ce8e52b66b7d3b6eca2a7d81e7f5b10a62"}, {"id": "b3ec8880-00df-3ffe-a894-ca7aeda4087f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b6cc9110-d0ce-3815-bb84-ca81f98f196f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bcda5833-25d0-37a1-9b67-ea6368acc068", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91fa127794ac1c48069479b9d45eb4c7378c0e30 <b722a607f858b9cd036075ea0efad553fb98e982"}, {"id": "be2d46f6-94d6-31f3-bfa4-4f6d7ed46583", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91fa127794ac1c48069479b9d45eb4c7378c0e30 <cbf0628c0b7db86c5ce36451f088101546acbf1d"}, {"id": "c0ff192c-9b21-378f-bcd8-7caa9748e645", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "242b80fd-1e6a-3b46-a2a7-63441907a8de", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}